<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Flax</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Flax is a plant grown for its fibres, which are made into linen, and for its seeds. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> valley supported intensive cultivation of cereals and flax under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>, and linen production was an important part of the Egyptian economy.</p></div>
